[00:20.50]1. When the eyes of blind ones see again
[00:27.26]And the ears of deaf ones hear again,
[00:34.08]When the songs of children fill the air
[00:40.60]And joy and peace are ev’rywhere,
[00:46.86]When our loved ones will return to life,
[00:53.78]To an earth that’s free from sin and strife,
[01:00.36](Chorus)
[01:00.46]You will see how God these things supplies,
[01:09.06]If you keep your eyes on the prize.
[01:29.72]2. When the wolves and lambs will feed as one,
[01:36.64]When the bears and calves bask in the sun,
[01:43.18]Then a mere young boy will lead them all,
[01:49.52]And they will heed his childish call.
[01:56.36]When our tears belong to yesterday,
[02:03.24]When our fears and pain have passed away,
[02:09.86](Chorus)
[02:10.34]You will see how God these things supplies,
[02:21.44]If you keep your eyes on the prize.
